{# Start here — a short, chosen list.

   Every other route into the writing is complete and neutral: all entries,
   all topics, all time, newest first. That answers "what is there?" and never
   "what's worth reading?", because recency is not a proxy for quality. This
   is the only list on the site ordered by judgement.

   Set on the entry itself:
     featured      — position in the list, 1 upward
     featured_note — one line on why it's here, in the first person

   Kept deliberately short. A list of fifteen picks is not a pick. #}
{%- set picks = collections.featured -%}
{%- if picks and picks.length -%}
<ol class="kh-picked">
  {%- for p in picks %}
  <li class="kh-picked__item">
    <span class="kh-picked__num" aria-hidden="true">{% if loop.index < 10 %}0{% endif %}{{ loop.index }}</span>
    <div class="kh-picked__body">
      <a class="kh-picked__link" href="{{ p.url | url }}">{{ p.data.title }}</a>
      {%- if p.data.featured_note %}
      <p class="kh-picked__note">{{ p.data.featured_note | emdash | safe }}</p>
      {%- endif %}
    </div>
    <span class="kh-meta kh-picked__date">{{ p.date | dateDisplay('y') }}</span>
  </li>
  {%- endfor %}
</ol>
{%- endif -%}
